1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,700
What the difference between paying fifty dollars with debit... and fifty dollars with credit?

2
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:06,225
Same fifty dollars.

3
00:00:06,225 --> 00:00:06,950
Today.

4
00:00:06,950 --> 00:00:08,000
This is Doug.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,450
Doug need new jacket.

6
00:00:09,450 --> 00:00:10,875
Puffin sell jacket.

7
00:00:10,875 --> 00:00:12,025
Fifty dollars.

8
00:00:12,025 --> 00:00:13,600
Doug pay with debit card.

9
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:14,287
Beep.

10
00:00:14,287 --> 00:00:16,725
Fifty dollars leave Doug bank account.

11
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:17,550
Right now.

12
00:00:17,550 --> 00:00:18,212
Done.

13
00:00:18,212 --> 00:00:18,987
Simple.

14
00:00:18,987 --> 00:00:21,587
Next winter, Doug pay with credit card.

15
00:00:21,587 --> 00:00:22,275
Beep.

16
00:00:22,275 --> 00:00:23,225
Doug account?

17
00:00:23,225 --> 00:00:24,212
Still full.

18
00:00:24,212 --> 00:00:26,512
Fox the Banker pay Puffin for Doug.

19
00:00:26,512 --> 00:00:28,650
Now Doug owe Fox fifty dollars.

20
00:00:28,650 --> 00:00:30,587
One month later, the bill come.

21
00:00:30,587 --> 00:00:34,887
If Doug pay all fifty dollars on time... interest: zero.

22
00:00:34,887 --> 00:00:36,337
Doug even get points.

23
00:00:36,337 --> 00:00:38,087
And his credit score can go up.

24
00:00:38,087 --> 00:00:39,037
Doug smart.

25
00:00:39,037 --> 00:00:40,787
But if Doug pay only a little...

26
00:00:40,787 --> 00:00:42,062
Fox add interest.

27
00:00:42,062 --> 00:00:43,062
Every month.

28
00:00:43,062 --> 00:00:47,525
In real life, average credit card interest is about twenty-two percent a year.

29
00:00:47,525 --> 00:00:49,212
That is Federal Reserve data.

30
00:00:49,212 --> 00:00:50,812
Fifty dollars for one year?

31
00:00:50,812 --> 00:00:53,000
Doug pay more than ten dollars extra.

32
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,387
One night, Stoat steal Doug card.

33
00:00:55,387 --> 00:00:56,275
With debit?

34
00:00:56,275 --> 00:00:57,575
Doug own money gone.

35
00:00:57,575 --> 00:00:58,962
Doug wait for the bank.

36
00:00:58,962 --> 00:00:59,887
With credit?

37
00:00:59,887 --> 00:01:01,062
It is Fox money.

38
00:01:01,062 --> 00:01:04,550
By law, Doug pay fifty dollars max. Usually zero.

39
00:01:04,550 --> 00:01:07,225
Debit: you spend only money you have.

40
00:01:07,225 --> 00:01:08,712
Credit: you borrow.

41
00:01:08,712 --> 00:01:11,537
Points and protection, but pay back in full.

42
00:01:11,537 --> 00:01:12,500
Same beep.

43
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:13,687
Very different bill.

44
00:01:13,687 --> 00:01:14,812
Debit or credit?

45
00:01:14,812 --> 00:01:15,987
Which one you use?

46
00:01:15,987 --> 00:01:17,637
Tell Doug in the comments.

